From: AirPods Control
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: add IMC Networks 13d3:3622 (MediaTek MT7922)

The ID is used by MT7922 combo cards (Windows: "MediaTek Bluetooth Adapter",
USB\VID_13D3&PID_3622). Without the entry btusb binds through the generic class
match and never runs the MediaTek setup (firmware download). Flags copied from
the neighbouring MT7922A entries.

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index 4c21230ae..a2a402ad2 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -685,6 +685,9 @@ static const struct usb_device_id quirks_table[] = {
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x13d3, 0x3607), .driver_info = BTUSB_MEDIATEK |
 						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH |
 						     BTUSB_VALID_LE_STATES },
+	{ USB_DEVICE(0x13d3, 0x3622), .driver_info = BTUSB_MEDIATEK |
+						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH |
+						     BTUSB_VALID_LE_STATES },
 
 	/* Additional MediaTek MT7925 Bluetooth devices */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x0489, 0xe111), .driver_info = BTUSB_MEDIATEK |
